questions.question_text:
Calculate the area of this shape, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\fill[blue!25] (0,0) -- (0,2) -- (3.5,2) arc[start angle=90,end angle=0,radius=2] -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (0,2) node[midway,left] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw[thick] (0,2) -- (3.5,2) node[midway,above] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\draw[thick] (3.5,2) arc[start angle=90,end angle=0,radius=2];
\draw[thick] (5.5,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[dashed] (3.5,0) -- (3.5,2);
\fill (3.5,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (4.5,0) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of this shape, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\fill[blue!25] (-1.75,0) -- (1.75,0) -- (0,1.5) -- cycle;
\fill[blue!25] (1.75,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-180,radius=1.75] -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (-1.75,0) -- (0,1.5) -- (1.75,0);
\draw[thick] (1.75,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-180,radius=1.75];
\draw[dashed] (-1.75,0) -- (1.75,0);
\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (-0.95,0.22) {$14\text{ mm}$};
\draw[<->] (0,0.05) -- (0,1.45) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A semicircle has been cut out of one end of this rectangle. Calculate the shaded area, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\fill[blue!25] (0,0) rectangle (3.85,2.1);
\fill[white] (3.85,2.1) arc[start angle=90,end angle=270,radius=1.05] -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (3.85,0) node[midway,below] {$11\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick] (0,2.1) -- (3.85,2.1);
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (0,2.1) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick] (3.85,0) -- (3.85,2.1);
\draw[thick] (3.85,2.1) arc[start angle=90,end angle=270,radius=1.05];
\fill (3.85,1.05) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[<->] (4.4,0) -- (4.4,2.1) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the shaded area, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\fill[blue!25] (0,0) circle (2.1);
\fill[white] (-2.1,0) -- (2.1,0) -- (0,2.1) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (2.1);
\draw[thick] (-2.1,0) -- (2.1,0) -- (0,2.1) -- cycle;
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (0,-0.32) {$14\text{ cm}$};
\draw[<->] (0,0.05) -- (0,2.05);
\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (0.45,1.05) {$7\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region is the ring between two circles with the same centre. Calculate its area in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\fill[blue!25] (0,0) circle (2.4);
\fill[white] (0,0) circle (1.44);
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (2.4);
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.44);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (140:2.4) node[midway,above,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$10\text{ mm}$};
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (-40:1.44) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$6\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A quadrant of radius $8$ m has been cut from two opposite corners of this square. Calculate the shaded area, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\fill[blue!25] (0,0) rectangle (3.2,3.2);
\fill[white] (0,0) -- (1.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=1.6] -- cycle;
\fill[white] (3.2,3.2) -- (1.6,3.2) arc[start angle=180,end angle=270,radius=1.6] -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,0) rectangle (3.2,3.2);
\draw[thick] (1.6,0) -- (3.2,0) -- (3.2,1.6);
\draw[thick] (0,1.6) -- (0,3.2) -- (1.6,3.2);
\draw[thick] (1.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=1.6];
\draw[thick] (1.6,3.2) arc[start angle=180,end angle=270,radius=1.6];
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (3.2,3.2) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[<->] (0,-0.5) -- (3.2,-0.5) node[midway,below] {$16\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of this shape in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\fill[blue!25] (0,0) rectangle (3.6,1.6);
\fill[blue!25] (3.6,0) arc[start angle=-90,end angle=90,radius=0.8] -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (3.6,0) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick] (0,1.6) -- (3.6,1.6);
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (0,1.6) node[midway,left] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick] (3.6,1.6) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,radius=0.8];
\fill (3.6,0.8) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (3.6,0.8) -- (4.4,0.8) node[midway,above] {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region lies between two sectors with the same centre and the same angle. Calculate its area, correct to the nearest square centimetre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\fill[blue!25] (0:2.4) arc[start angle=0,end angle=300,radius=2.4] -- (300:0.9) arc[start angle=300,end angle=0,radius=0.9] -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (0:0.9) -- (0:2.4);
\draw[thick] (300:0.9) -- (300:2.4);
\draw[thick] (0:2.4) arc[start angle=0,end angle=300,radius=2.4];
\draw[thick] (0:0.9) arc[start angle=0,end angle=300,radius=0.9];
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (75:0.9) node[midway,left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (180:2.4) node[midway,above,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0:0.45) arc[start angle=0,end angle=300,radius=0.45];
\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (150:0.75) {$300^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
